  "note": "Same-scope independent rejudgment against RFC 4271 Sections 9.1.2 and 9.1.2.1: unresolvable routes SHALL be removed from both the Loc-RIB and the routing table. Re-read every tagged cover, the actual retained-input unit, both ordinary real-socket daemon carriers, their complete shared scenario and observer helpers, the current selection/subscriber/mirroring/removal path, sysrib withdrawal generation and fib-kernel removal handling. The unit requires initial installation of the reachable preference, installation of the still-reachable fallback after one cover disappears, complete Loc-RIB absence after both disappear, retention of both received paths and recovery when a cover returns without another UPDATE. Read both accepted renewed unit receipts: omitting only no-candidate Loc-RIB removal passes initial preference and fallback, then fails exact absence at line 319; suppressing replacement mirroring passes initial selection, then fails reachable fallback at line 314. The latter fault does not reach the all-unresolved or restoration checks. Both internal and forked daemon placements receive actual BGP UPDATEs, prove the configured selecting-RIB process placement, and require BGP-best absence and zero Loc-RIB candidate rows before an exact zero-route kernel result across all tables can pass. Query or transport errors cannot count as absence. Their retained positive records disable only live fibKernel.processEvent withdrawal handling: the clean full lifecycle passes; the broken run passes the BGP-best and Loc-RIB absence gates, then fails on the remaining proto-250 subject route. Each retained negative CI record rejects terminal connected reachability and fails the initially legitimate direct BGP control while preserving the initial explicitly-gateway-resolved subject; it does not separately discriminate post-loss preservation or restoration. Clean lifecycle assertions still require the direct control after loss and recovery, and cover restoration must recover retained subject input without UPDATE. Shutdown is joined and every Ze route must be gone while the fixture link and OS connected route still exist, so owned link deletion cannot manufacture the live absence proof. Current source removes the no-candidate Loc-RIB contribution before best withdrawal publication; internal removal calls RIB.Remove, forked removal synchronously flushes RouteRemove, sysrib emits an outstanding programmed route's withdrawal and fib-kernel deletes the installed route. Explicit gateway/device fixture routes still take that path; suppression of otherwise valid targetless output does not substitute for withdrawal. The old CIs gained only an additional 3.1-2 comment and preserve every old tag and assertion. Independently parsed the final native freshness receipt: all six covers are fresh, zero stale and zero unproven, including the two renewed current checkRouteBestChange records. Both removal destinations and feasible fallback/preservation are enforced in this bounded IPv4 internal/forked topology. The helper/producer inventory is bound, and no later broken restoration success, packet-forwarding proof or new prospective-integration claim is inferred.",
